  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_05cb7e63082444629266d95057b4627f",
      "statement": "Brijio's core trust assumptions are that the user explicitly starts and controls the browser connection, authentication tokens are held only by authorized parties (separate MCP auth tokens for server/relay and a pairing token for relay/extension), the browser session belongs to the user, and the relay transports messages without needing to inspect content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/THREAT_MODEL.md#L55-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1c1e36c94cbb0280c8c56c15f273aad6bf53df8e6a4eabe34f0dfa1b6eab4ce9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md#L22-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f565263ca2f5e1ad6a144f7f370a0d8a0524ba6507ab73ecf576ef64f12de011:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2f43c2c799b44fd999c8d9fa45c0a03d",
      "statement": "Trust is bounded across four interfaces: Agent↔MCP server (MCP validates all requests, does not trust agent intent), MCP server↔relay (authenticated with separate tokens, relay need not inspect payloads), relay↔extension (pairing-token authenticated, extension does not trust relay confidentiality; E2E planned), and extension↔browser (extension runs with user-granted permissions, reads page content as data rather than executing it).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md#L45-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:029ebe98b51306c5660821ce4575c4a7f198786d644a92a3913ccfa2e68c8929:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md#L8-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e49ab0a711b5f1577b42df8b2572f1157fdd1a89928dff2dd56b8e4efd1e1d0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c2db191d4f56491f92c626611c2d0d89",
      "statement": "The threat model defines four attacker classes — malicious agent, compromised relay server, network attacker, and malicious website — each mitigated architecturally: explicit request/response protocol, no continuous streaming, user-controlled connection, progressive disclosure, least-privilege extension permissions, TLS, and planned E2E encryption.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/THREAT_MODEL.md#L13-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7e41f2f78009bb3a9c2076ee66ebdd4424e5f4906978c1a43b00436db1a5c13d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f66e0cf7d7224fb4adbd5b848cc94af4",
      "statement": "Brijio intentionally does not provide cookie export, session cloning, browser mirroring/remote desktop, continuous screenshots, continuous DOM streaming, background surveillance, browser history collection, credential extraction, or MFA interception; these are deliberate product boundaries (intentionally unsupported in the capability matrix), not missing features.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L40-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:809169498b4f65625b20da68e5f80e935aae8d733565d892885a96a5f797db61:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/project/CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md#L173-L188",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83ee070f427010a71239c1765ab1432c04b2159a45463312bafb0d99e9172b21:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/SECURITY_GUARANTEES.md#L1-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3626a37f667d817cce96ac5aba03bb25c6183302efe00e7bd3aadc3e93b32472:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f6ff019a19f64b7ba6ae15f2d2d93045",
      "statement": "AGENTS.md codifies non-negotiable product invariants: the user explicitly starts/stops the bridge, browser state is available only while the extension is connected, every read/action is initiated by an explicit MCP request, no continuous streaming or background surveillance, no cookie export/credential extraction/session cloning/MFA interception, preserve user-visible connection state and client-side action approval without bypassing approval checks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L40-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:809169498b4f65625b20da68e5f80e935aae8d733565d892885a96a5f797db61:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_45b33ee0123446368d219093dc1281c5",
      "statement": "Client-side action approval (ADR 0048) requires user approval only for a hardcoded set — submit_form, fetch_resource, and download_file — evaluated through a requiresApproval(operation) function; every approval-gated operation carries a unique actionUUID and approvalRequest flag.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L29-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fdf109051f3197a80b79db2d000f9ce505dfbe4d550226a461d7a506c59570f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a5afd9b7c84e4db4b538a5b78e7d40b3",
      "statement": "Approval pending actions and session grants are held in extension background memory only (never persistent storage), scoped to {origin, actionType}, verified against active tab origin at execution time, and cleared when the bridge disconnects, the extension reloads, or the browser session ends.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L131-L149",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e7ab103e316d196d24f41651054903d4d633ec3f8ba18de94aa1bcb7bcd0c029:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L38-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a96dd5a6b24aa1980972ca6cc79ad5631c555c8e0288a78522074e3512e7dfa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6bcc800a46064513b7d57170573b6feb",
      "statement": "The approval timeout is computed as httpRequestTimeoutMs minus a buffer so Brijio returns a structured approval_timeout error before the HTTP request times out; remote deployments must configure it below the shortest client/proxy/gateway/load-balancer timeout.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L151-L180",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2dc3200f1b7e506f8cbaf8b26a119c92558212008bc1f394ddd2b10ddfe4a46e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e519ef87a04e494e9e900dd7cca2de67",
      "statement": "Approval failures return structured error codes — approval_denied, approval_timeout, approval_unavailable (banner could not render), and approval_origin_changed — each carrying the relevant actionUUID; in batches denial is a focused per-action outcome and timeout yields a partial batch_result.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L220-L270",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:957550aca067468056826c785a8e944e50b21307b91304705cda2312fd020723:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L280-L298",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:35143c57e4b13544565f2e1bd3fcdcc2beb0fabf9ea4ce155913ff9bd5a01354:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_170b21a4304643778bc3e6103d747067",
      "statement": "The relay is intended as transport rather than a data processor: keepalive messages contain no browser state and the extension is reactive, answering explicit requests and returning structured results rather than publishing ambient state.",
